Title: The Misfortune of Meaning
Credit: Written by Lee Brandt
Draft date: September 2025

FADE IN:

INT. CHARLES’ APARTMENT – NIGHT

CHARLES HONEYCUTT pecks at a typewriter. Noir-style voiceover. Frozen mac & cheese. Stained robe.

        CHARLES (V.O.)
    They say every man has a story. Mine just never seemed to sell.

INT. PAGE TURNERS PUBLISHING – DAY

Stacks of books. QUEENIE oversees the fencing op. EDDIE works with tech. REECEY works the phones.

        QUEENIE
    Ship ten cases to the Goldstein drop. Mark 'em as bulk orders from a university.

INT. ART GALLERY – NIGHT

Rich weirdos misread Charles’ novel as postmodern genius.

        SNOBBY WOMAN
    “The shadows stretched long... like the disappointment in his father's voice.”

INT. PAGE TURNERS HQ – NIGHT

A BookTuber puts Charles’ book on a viral list.

        YOUTUBER (ON SCREEN)
    It’s like Bukowski ghostwrote for Black Mirror and gave up halfway through. Five stars.

INT. CHARLES’ APARTMENT – NIGHT

Charles celebrates a royalty check. Has no idea it's cartel money.

INT. FEDERAL TASK FORCE OFFICE – DAY

LT. HARPER pins photos to a board. Red string. Trouble brewing.

INT. GALA – NIGHT

High society event. CHARLES gives a live reading.

        CHARLES
    And that’s when the bullet hit the statue...

BANG. CARTEL HITMAN shoots KEVIN HART GUY.

INT. INTERROGATION ROOM – DAY

QUEENIE cuts a deal with the feds.

        QUEENIE
    We stole from Wal-Mart with body counts. Let us help bring them down.

INT. SAFEHOUSE MONTAGE – VARIOUS

New identities. New lives. Family gets out.

INT. BOOKSTORE – DAY

Charles signs _The Honeycutt Affair_.

        FAN
    Is it based on a true story?

        CHARLES
    Writers write what they know.

INT. SUBURBAN LIVING ROOM – NIGHT

KEVIN HART GUY alive. Desk duty. Tucks in his kids.

        KEVIN
    Missed bedtime. Glad to be home.

FADE OUT.